      "document_hash": "6158348c51376ab74d1db5c527db75dc1f6fae458381a8602802fefed89b5057",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6158348c5137-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "This Court has made clear that conspiracy is an inchoate offense, the essence of which is the agreement to commit an unlawful act."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1184",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6158348c51376ab74d1db5c527db75dc1f6fae458381a8602802fefed89b5057",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6158348c5137-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: And taken some act in furtherance of it?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1184",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6158348c51376ab74d1db5c527db75dc1f6fae458381a8602802fefed89b5057",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6158348c5137-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: When does the conspiracy terminate, in your view?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1184",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6158348c51376ab74d1db5c527db75dc1f6fae458381a8602802fefed89b5057",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6158348c5137-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 8,
        "start": 8
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Conspiracy to distribute and deliver marijuana and cocaine."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1184",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6158348c51376ab74d1db5c527db75dc1f6fae458381a8602802fefed89b5057",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6158348c5137-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: And the difference between an attempt and the conspiracy, in the attempt you need a dangerous probability of success or something along that line, but you don't need that in a conspiracy case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice (unspecified)",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1184",
      "confidence": 0.85,
      "document_hash": "6158348c51376ab74d1db5c527db75dc1f6fae458381a8602802fefed89b5057",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6158348c5137-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: No, I'm not thinking of that. I'm thinking it is an -- there -- there is no reason to think -- all we know about him is he's arrested and he happens to mention something to a neighbor that has nothing to do -- who has nothing to do with the conspiracy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Dreeben",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1184",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "6158348c51376ab74d1db5c527db75dc1f6fae458381a8602802fefed89b5057",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6158348c5137-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. DREEBEN: Right. The statement to be admitted as a statement of a co-conspirator must be both during the course of and in furtherance of the conspiracy."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Shurtliff (Respondents)",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1184",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "6158348c51376ab74d1db5c527db75dc1f6fae458381a8602802fefed89b5057",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6158348c5137-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. SHURTLIFF: Mr. Chief Justice, may it please the Court, counsel: Mr. Sullivan and I expect that we were not invited here to argue our view that the case below was decided on the sufficiency of the evidence question. However, having said that, we would not wish to have it taken that we abandon that argument."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1184",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6158348c51376ab74d1db5c527db75dc1f6fae458381a8602802fefed89b5057",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6158348c5137-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: Is that the argument?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1184",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6158348c51376ab74d1db5c527db75dc1f6fae458381a8602802fefed89b5057",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6158348c5137-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "QUESTION: May I ask? Are the -- are the instructions to the jury in the papers before us?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2002-01-1184",
